# Private working documents such as TODOs and design notes; publishable docs belong elsewhere
docs/
# Vidlab: milestone evidence, architecture answers and the licence table are the
# acceptance record for this fork, so they are tracked even though the base keeps
# docs/ private. Everything else under docs/ stays ignored.
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/milestone0-*.md
!docs/milestone-a*.md
!docs/milestone-b*.md
!docs/milestone-c*.md
!docs/licence-table.md
# The allow-list rules are the operating manual for the i18n dangerous-class check,
# so a reviewer needs them beside the code that enforces them.
!docs/i18n-allowlist.md
# Project rules the gates enforce (source size ceiling, where downloaded data
# lives). A reviewer must be able to read the rule without reading the gate.
!docs/engineering-rules.md
# D-slice rulings (kill policy, admission gate, artifact placement, transport).
# D1b and D2 consume these decisions instead of re-deriving them from the code.
!docs/d-job-implementation.md
# AV1's acceptance record: the owned behaviour of detach/merge, including the
# merge side effects a reviewer has to be able to check against the code.
!docs/av1-audio-detach.md
!docs/evidence/
docs/evidence/*
!docs/evidence/*.md
!docs/evidence/*.png
!docs/evidence/*.mjs
!docs/evidence/*.mp4
!docs/evidence/*.json
!docs/evidence/*.txt
# Local model-optimization plan / notes (was mistakenly committed; keep out of the public repo)
MODEL-OPT-PLAN.md
/MODEL-OPT-PLAN*/
*.opt-plan.md

# Keep local and temporary check scripts out of the repository; stable regressions use *.verify.* via npm test.
*.check.ts
*.check.mjs
# Keep the external MCP bridge protocol regression with its implementation; the legacy name is intentional.
!server/external-agent/broker.check.ts

# Local development and verification scripts.
# `/scripts/*` rather than `/scripts/`: git never re-includes files inside an
# ignored DIRECTORY, so with the old form every `!` line below was inert and
# new canonical scripts could only enter the repo via `git add -f` — a new
# scripts/*.verify.mjs registered in package.json was silently skipped by
# `git add -A`, and CI died with MODULE_NOT_FOUND on a file that exists locally.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/sync-mediapipe.mjs
# Stable regressions are *.verify.* by convention (see the *.check.* rule
# above), so they are never local-only.
!/scripts/*.verify.mjs
!/scripts/*.verify.ts
# The production start (A1) and the release/rollback tool are part of the
# product, not local scratch: the service wrapper in A2 runs serve-prod.mjs and
# the release check imports the harness beside it.
!/scripts/serve-prod.mjs
!/scripts/release.mjs
!/scripts/a1-harness.mjs
# The milestone-C harness the C verifies import (a1-harness.mjs's counterpart).
!/scripts/c-harness.ts
# The i18n allow-list policy both i18n checks import (i18n-allowlist.verify.mjs
# and check-i18n.mjs). A shared module, not a local scratch script: if it is not
# tracked, both checks die with MODULE_NOT_FOUND on a checkout.
!/scripts/i18n-allowlist-rules.mjs
# The D3 exit-test measurement tool (word error rate against a reference the owner
# supplies). It is a deliverable, not local scratch: the owner and a reviewer both
# run it, so it has to be in the checkout. Its unit suite is a *.verify.ts and is
# re-included by the rule above.
!/scripts/wer.ts
# The D5 LUT generator. The committed assets/luts/*.cube files are its output, so a
# fresh checkout must be able to rebuild them byte for byte — the same reason
# sync-mediapipe.mjs is tracked. Its check is scripts/looks.verify.mjs (re-included
# by the *.verify.mjs rule above).
!/scripts/generate-looks.mjs

